<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/1-02416172a39b070e> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[OCL] Add multiplicity constraint:" ;
    skos:definition "[OCL] Add multiplicity constraint: choose this option if there is a domain restriction that requires an instance of Source, or of one of its subtypes, to be connected to a minimum, maximum or precise number of instances of Target, or one of its subtypes. The following OCL invariant enforces the desired constraint: [figure: context Source ] inv: let sub1Size = self.target->select( x [figure: ] x.oclIsTypeOf(_'Target Subtype-1'))->size() | in sub1Size >= min1 and sub1Size <= max1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/ImpAbs/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 1 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[OCL] Add multiplicity constraint:** choose this option if there is a domain restriction that requires an instance of Source, or of one of its subtypes, to be connected to a minimum, maximum or precise number of instances of Target, or one of its subtypes. The following OCL invariant enforces the desired constraint:
		
			| *context Source*
			| *inv: let sub1Size = self.target->select( x |*
			| *x.oclIsTypeOf(_'Target Subtype-1'))->size()*
			| *in sub1Size >= min1 and sub1Size <= max1*""" .

