    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/DecInt/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[Mod/Del] Invert/Delete Generalization:** consists of deleting and/or inverting one or more generalizations from Type to one of the identified parents." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-0e146a7f8f80103b> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[New] Create dependency between relators:" ;
    skos:definition "[New] Create dependency between relators: Create formal relations connecting relators that depend on one another. This solution generates an occurrence of AssCyc (which the user should be analyzed) and an occurrence of UndefFormal (which the user can ignore)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/MultDep/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[New] Create dependency between relators:** Create formal relations connecting relators that depend on one another. This solution generates an occurrence of AssCyc (which the user should be analyzed) and an occurrence of UndefFormal (which the user can ignore)." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-3d5eaa785e6c671f> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[New] Add custom meta-property (subsetting association):" ;
    skos:definition "[New] Add custom meta-property (subsetting association): choose this option if the relation between Source and Target have particular meta-properties (like isReadOnly and isEssential) when an instance of Source, or of one of its subtypes, to be connected to a minimum, maximum or precise number of instances of Target, or one of its subtypes." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/ImpAbs/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText "**[New] Add custom meta-property (subsetting association):** choose this option if the relation between Source and Target have particular meta-properties (like isReadOnly and isEssential) when an instance of Source, or of one of its subtypes, to be connected to a minimum, maximum or precise number of instances of Target, or one of its subtypes." .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-66cc3b9b19100913> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[New/Mod] Disjoint parts:" ;
    skos:definition "[New/Mod] Disjoint parts: Enforce part types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set. Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/WholeOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[New/Mod] Disjoint parts:** Enforce part types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set.
		
		* *Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-6f39fc7ee8ad82e7> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod/New] Disjoint whole:" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod/New] Disjoint whole: Enforce whole types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set. Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/PartOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[Mod/New] Disjoint whole:** Enforce whole types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set.
		
		* *Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-70a19ce231de1c6a> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[OCL] Set Left Universal Composition:" ;
    skos:definition "[OCL] Set Left Universal Composition: add an OCL invariant to enforce that type B has a left universal composition to type A: [figure: context BSource ] inv: self.bTarget->asSet()->forAll( y [figure: ] ASource.allInstances()->forAll( z [figure: ] z.aTarget->asSet()->contains(y) implies | z.aTarget->asSet()->contains(self))" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/RelComp/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[OCL] Set Left Universal Composition:** add an OCL invariant to enforce that type B has a left universal composition to type A:
		
		| *context BSource*
		| *inv: self.bTarget->asSet()->forAll( y |*
		| 	*ASource.allInstances()->forAll( z |*
		| 		*z.aTarget->asSet()->contains(y) implies*
		| 		*z.aTarget->asSet()->contains(self))*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-86506cb9cac4965d> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod/New] Disjoint mediated" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod/New] Disjoint mediated: Enforce types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set. \\ Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/RelOver/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[Mod/New] Disjoint mediated**: Enforce types to be disjoint through the creation or alteration of a disjoint generalization set.
		
		\\* *Note: to make all types exclusive, every binary combination should be explicitly ruled out*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-8fa1bfa57ab1b943> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod] Set as mode:" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod] Set as mode: choose this plan when RigidType-n is in fact an unstructured property of Relator-n. This is only true if the existential dependency specified in the mediation is reversed (RigidType-n should depend on «relator» and not the other way around)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/RelRig/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:references ontouml:relator ;
    ok:sourceText "**[Mod] Set as mode:** choose this plan when RigidType-n is in fact an unstructured property of Relator-n. This is only true if the existential dependency specified in the mediation is reversed (RigidType-n should depend on «:ref:`relator`» and not the other way around)" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-98f8c9d868edec03> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[Mod/New] Disjoint:" ;
    skos:definition "[Mod/New] Disjoint: this action should be taken if being related through B implies not being related through A. Differently from the first two, this constraint can only be enforce through OCL invariants: [figure: context BSource ] inv subset : self.oclAsType(ASource).aTarget->excludesAll( self.bTarget.oclAsType(ATarget)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/RelSpec/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[Mod/New] Disjoint:** this action should be taken if being related through B implies not being related through A. Differently from the first two, this constraint can only be enforce through OCL invariants:
	
			| *context BSource*
			| *inv subset : self.oclAsType(ASource).aTarget->excludesAll( self.bTarget.oclAsType(ATarget)*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-9f206a557c2041cd> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[OCL]" ;
    skos:definition "[OCL] Define uniqueness constraint (Historical Relator): this plan applies to a combination of the mediations and, although it can be applied more than once for different combinations, it cannot be applied simultaneously with the current relator plan. [figure: context Relator ] inv: Relator.allInstances()->select( r [figure: r<>self and r.type1=self.type1 ] and r.type2=self.type2 and concurrent(self,r))-> size()=<n-1> [figure: ] context Relator::concurrent(r:Relator):Boolean [figure: body: self.start = r.start or (self.start<r.start and r.start<self.end) ] or (r.start<self.start and self.start<r.end)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/RepRel/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:references ontouml:relator ;
    ok:sourceText """**[OCL]** Define uniqueness constraint (Historical Relator): this plan applies to a combination of the mediations and, although it can be applied more than once for different combinations, it cannot be applied simultaneously with the current :ref:`relator<relator>` plan.
	
			| *context Relator*
			| *inv: Relator.allInstances()->select( r | r<>self and r.type1=self.type1*
			| *and r.type2=self.type2 and concurrent(self,r))-> size()=<n-1>*
			|
			| *context Relator::concurrent(r:Relator):Boolean*
			| *body: self.start = r.start or (self.start<r.start and r.start<self.end)*
			| *or (r.start<self.start and self.start<r.end)*""" .

<https://w3id.org/ontouml/knowledge#refactoring/3-ac5de3701e0a2d25> a ok:RefactoringPlan ;
    rdfs:label "[New/Mod] Implicit rigid subtype:" ;
    skos:definition "[New/Mod] Implicit rigid subtype: create rigid subtypes that are the new direct parents of one or more anti-rigid subtypes. If only one rigid subtype is created, the modeler can optionally set it as derived by negation of the other rigid subtypes. The following OCL template is proposed to achieve that: [figure: context NewRigid::allInstances() : Set(NewRigid) ] derive : RigidParent.allInstances()->select( x [figure: not(x.oclIsTypeOf(Rigid:subscript:`1` ) or ] x.oclsIsTypeOf(Rigid:subscript:`2` ) or … or x.oclIsTypeOf(Rigid:subscript:`n` ))" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:ontouml:source:anti-patterns/anti-patterns/HetColl/index.rst> ;
    ok:order 3 ;
    ok:sourceText """**[New/Mod] Implicit rigid subtype:** create rigid subtypes that are the new direct parents of one or more anti-rigid subtypes. If only one rigid subtype is created, the modeler can optionally set it as derived by negation of the other rigid subtypes. The following OCL template is proposed to achieve that:
	
			| *context NewRigid::allInstances() : Set(NewRigid)*
			| *derive : RigidParent.allInstances()->select( x | not(x.oclIsTypeOf(Rigid*:subscript:`1` *) or*
			| *x.oclsIsTypeOf(Rigid*:subscript:`2` *) or … or x.oclIsTypeOf(Rigid*:subscript:`n` *))*""" .

